      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "What is the $3$rd term of the geometric sequence given below?\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-5{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{75},\\,n\\ge 1\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the recursive formula to compute the terms of the sequence up to the $3$rd term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{75} \\\\ {a}_{2} & =-5{a}_{1}=-5(\\frac{1}{75})=-\\frac{1}{15} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =-5{a}_{2}=-5(-\\frac{1}{15})=\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${a}_{3}=\\frac{1}{3}.$",
